    "result_text": "The build is green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `ageBand` feature for `POST /api/owners` (returned via `GET /api/owners/{id}`), computing an owner's age band from an optional `birthDate` against their `registrationDate`.\n\nFollowing the project's OpenAPI-generated-DTO + MapStruct + OfficeFloor conventions, no new function class was needed \u2014 `ageBand` is a derived field that the single Owner\u2192DTO mapper boundary carries automatically, exactly like the existing `locality`/`contactPreference`/`bulkSignupWarning` fields.\n\nChanges:\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (optional, `format: date`) to `OwnerFields` (so it's accepted on input and echoed back), and a read-only `ageBand` string to the `Owner` response schema.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `birthDate` column (`@Column(name = \"birth_date\")`) with accessors, and a `@Transient getAgeBand()` returning `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), `SENIOR` (65+) via `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate)`, or `null` when `birthDate` is absent.\n- **DB schemas** \u2014 added `birth_date DATE` to the `owners` table in the hsqldb, h2, mysql, and postgres `schema.sql` files (hsqldb is the one the test suite uses).\n\nMapStruct picks up `birthDate` (request\u2192entity) and `birthDate`/`ageBand` (entity\u2192response) by name automatically, so the mapper and pipeline YAML were untouched.\n\nTests: `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 the new `coreDerivesAgeBand` acceptance test (birthDate 1990-01-01 \u2192 `ADULT`) passes.",
