    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is a clean, additive extension that mirrors the model's established conventions.\n\n- `getAgeBand()` follows the exact pattern already set by `getLocality()` and `getContactPreference()` (`Owner.java:300`, `Owner.java:328`): a `@Transient` derived read-only property, same Javadoc style (\"Not persisted \u2014 derived from ...\"), same null/guard handling. Placing the age-band logic as a derived accessor on `Owner` \u2014 rather than inventing a new helper class or putting it in a pipeline step \u2014 is the natural fit here, since it's purely a function of two fields already on the entity.\n- `birthDate` field + getter/setter are placed adjacent to the closely-related `registrationDate`, and the ordering is consistent with the four schema files.\n- Schema additions are applied uniformly across h2/hsqldb/mysql/postgres, and the openapi additions (request `birthDate`, read-only response `ageBand`) are consistent with how other derived fields like `contactPreference` are documented.\n\nNo duplication, no catch-all accumulation, logic sits in the right unit. A maintainer would find this natural.\n\n(Non-structural nit, outside this review's scope: the postgres `schema.sql` `birth_date` line is indented with fewer spaces than its neighbors \u2014 purely cosmetic alignment, not a structural concern.)",
